      "summary": "Former French politician François Fillon has been suspended from the Legion of Honor and the National Order of Merit for ten years, more than a year after his conviction in the \"Penelopegate\" scandal involving fictitious employment positions. The suspension was imposed by governmental decree following his legal condemnation for the scheme.",
      "takeaway": "A former prime minister and presidential candidate loses his honors a year after conviction, ending a chapter in France's most serious recent political integrity scandal.",
      "why_it_matters": "The suspension strips Fillon of honors that symbolize official recognition of his public service, marking the completion of legal consequences for the scandal that destroyed his 2017 presidential campaign and damaged confidence in French political institutions."
